        "id": 1967151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-09T22:51:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The hook implements the same functionality as what has been moved into the block. Normally `arg[1]` holds the file name and length, but since tempfiles are anonymous, there is no `arg[1]` here. Thus, we always BUG on `in_args !\u003d 2` because `in_args` will always be 1. The main purpose for this `BUG_ON` seems to be to prevent the `in_numargs` and `in_args` from getting set incorrectly below, but since the vendor hook sets these values (and the FUSE server on the host parses 2 args instead of 3 for tmpfiles). This seemed like a reasonable way to have the correct functionality without affecting the standard code path, but maybe we can find a better solution.",
      "parentUuid": "04886771_21fcffa0",
      "revId": "842037ecc88c307259f10643c7f2fcfb14e4865a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
